### [3D Musings]($section.id('2024-12-29T00:00:00'))

Now in 3D!

### [Christmas Crafting Days!]($section.id('2024-12-25T00:00:00'))

I create a cardboard prototype of what i envision the computer to look like. it's slighty too short on the top-right dimension, but apart from that i'm pretty happy witht the overall layout 

Modules left to right:
- Mainboard with display, two buttons, usb-c for programming/debugging and usb-a for devices
- high-end video card with hdmi, vga and rca/cvbs
- stereo audio in/out with audio on pairs of rca
- 4-port usb card
- 2-port rs232
- 2-port C64 serial
- DIY board with a perfboard inside
- digital and analog I/O on pin headers

### [Framing the case]($section.id('2024-11-21T00:00:00'))

i dont have time to code much, but i'm sketching out the case for the home computer

the mug is the ikea standard mug, for size reference. the computer will get 7 expansion slots, one which can do video, and one which can do audio

### [The beginning of a new era]($section.id("2024-09-05T00:00:00"))

some different mental tasks ahead:
planning the Ashet Home Computer™, Mark 4.

This is a rough sketch of the mainboard, and it's all built around the absent RP2350 Stamp XL, which should be possible to clip into the large hole in the middle
